 ## Background
-Originated in the context of text-driven 3D face manipulation using deformable Neural Radiance Fields (FaceCLIPNeRF) [S1]. The method was introduced to address the issue that interpolated latent codes between learned codes often produce visually unnatural deformations [S1]. It builds on the idea that bounding the Lipschitz constant of the scene manipulator MLP ensures that small changes in latent codes result in small, controlled changes in the output, leading to more plausible deformations [S1].
